2. The fundamental architectural separation

This is now the most important separation in the entire system:

$$ \boxed{ Authoritative\ State \neq Derived\ Assessment \neq Governance\ Decision } $$
Authoritative State

Things that happened or were explicitly recorded:

evidence;
source;
identity;
context;
semantic contract;
event;
provenance;
temporal validity;
revision.
Derived Assessment

Things calculated from the state:

semantic assessment;
dependency assessment;
conflict assessment;
uncertainty assessment;
knowledge attribution;
TPP;
identifiability;
determination;
stopping assessment.
Governance State

Things authorized by an institution:

permission;
decision;
