approval;
selection;
accountability.

This separation should be enforced in the code.

3. C4 is important — but we must use it correctly

One critical DDD/C4 distinction:

A C4 Container is not the same thing as a DDD Bounded Context.

A C4 container means a separately deployable/runtime application, database, or other technology boundary.

A DDD bounded context means:

a boundary within which a particular domain model and language have consistent meaning.

Therefore:

C4 Container ≠ DDD Bounded Context

We must not create one microservice for every KnowledgeOS layer.

That would be architectural overengineering.

