14. Knowledge Attribution

The canonical implementation should be:

$$ KA_t(a,p)= Assess_{KAC}(E_t,a,p,C_t,\Gamma_t,t) $$

The code should therefore look conceptually like:

KnowledgeAttributionAssessment assess(
    EpistemicState state,
    AgentId agent,
    PropositionId proposition,
    KnowledgeAttributionContract contract,
    SemanticRegime regime,
    Context context,
    Instant time
)

It returns:

Established
Rejected
Unknown
Conditional
Expired
NotApplicable

It does not mutate the proposition.

15. Determination Service

The Determination Service consumes:

Evidence
Dependency Assessments
Conflict Assessments
Uncertainty Assessments
Semantic Assessments
Model Assessments
Contract
Inquiry

and produces:

$$ Determination. $$

Conceptually:

Determination determine(
    Inquiry inquiry,
    EpistemicState state,
    AssessmentSet assessments,
    DeterminationContract contract
)

The result may be:

NONE
UNIQUE
MULTIPLE
BLOCKED
