49. Dependency rule

The dependency direction should be:

interfaces
    ↓
application
    ↓
domain
    ↓
kernel

Infrastructure points inward through ports:

domain ← ports ← infrastructure adapters

Never:

domain → PostgreSQL
domain → OpenAI
domain → XGBoost
domain → REST
50. Formal engine should be pure where possible

For example:

$$ TPP(\pi,Z,W) $$

should ideally be a pure function.

Similarly:

$$ Compose(T_1,T_2,C) $$

should be pure.

This makes:

testing;
reproducibility;
formal verification;
caching;
reference comparison

much easier.

51. Event-driven integration

Internally, domain events can be used:

EvidenceRecorded
       ↓
AssessmentRequested
       ↓
AssessmentProduced
       ↓
DeterminationRecomputed

But we should not introduce Kafka immediately.

Spring application events or transactional outbox are sufficient initially.

Kafka becomes appropriate when we actually have:

high event volume;
independent consumers;
asynchronous ML;
distributed integration.
52. Transactional boundary

A particularly important transaction:

Record Evidence
+
Record Provenance
+
Publish EvidenceRecorded

must be atomic.

Use the transactional outbox pattern if external event publication is required.

This is consistent with your previous architecture experience.

53. Versioning

Every semantic/logic/regime contract should be versioned:

$$ Contract_{v1} $$ $$ Contract_{v2} $$

An assessment must always record:

$$ ContractVersion. $$

Otherwise historical reconstruction becomes impossible.

54. Temporal model

Store at least:

$$ OccurredAt $$

and:

$$ RecordedAt. $$

These are different.

Example:

Evidence occurred on Monday but was entered on Wednesday.

KnowledgeOS must preserve both.

55. Provenance model

At minimum:

$$ Provenance= (Source, Agent, Time, Parent, Transformation, Contract, Version). $$

For ML:

$$ ModelVersion $$

must also be recorded.

For generated evidence:

$$ GenerationMethod $$

must be explicit.

56. AI-generated epistemic objects

This is particularly important.

AI output must carry:

origin = AI
modelId
modelVersion
prompt/context contract
generationTime
inputReferences
confidence
candidateStatus

and:

$$ \boxed{ AI\text{-}generated\ Claim \neq Authoritative\ Evidence } $$

unless explicitly admitted under a contract.

57. Final architecture principle

The system should never ask:

“Is this object knowledge?”

without also asking:

Knowledge of whom?
About what?
At what time?
Under which context?
Under which semantic regime?
Under which evidence contract?
Under which authority?
For which inquiry?
With which provenance?

That is why the KnowledgeOS architecture is fundamentally multi-dimensional.

